WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[theme music playing]

01:03.229 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:07.358 --> 01:10.403
-So, what are you saying?
-There's something I do want.

01:10.487 --> 01:12.697
I've thought of something
I don't want taken away.

01:12.781 --> 01:13.907
Grandma.

01:14.657 --> 01:15.492
Huh?

01:16.159 --> 01:16.993
Pan-geum?

01:17.786 --> 01:20.455
-I am ready to make my second wish.
-Whoa, wait, wait, wait.

01:21.122 --> 01:23.166
Just think about it carefully.

01:24.709 --> 01:26.795
Think long and hard about this calmly.

01:27.420 --> 01:29.964
Are you really willing
to give up your soul for this?

01:33.384 --> 01:37.889
I want Grandma young.
So make Pan-geum my exact age.

01:39.390 --> 01:42.519
That's it. This will be the second wish.

01:45.063 --> 01:46.898
-[scoffs]
-But not immediately.

01:46.981 --> 01:47.982
Tomorrow's the wake.

01:50.026 --> 01:52.904
Fulfill it in… three days, precisely.

01:54.948 --> 01:56.950
You're scheduling your wish?

02:01.412 --> 02:02.747
-Hawaii?
-[Ka-young] Mm.

02:03.373 --> 02:06.459
Yes, we are going to Hawaii.
Some fresh air. We fly in three days.

02:06.543 --> 02:09.045
-Monday.
-On Monday? But there's so much to do--

02:09.129 --> 02:11.798
It's all been planned.
All you have to do is join me.

02:12.841 --> 02:15.135
I bought the tickets already.
Non-refundable.

02:15.218 --> 02:18.138
Already? Oh, wow. Oh, well, in that case…

02:18.847 --> 02:21.266
In that case,
we can't let these go to waste.

02:22.308 --> 02:24.018
We have to go, of course we do.

02:24.644 --> 02:28.064
My goodness. Ka-young, am I dreaming?

02:28.148 --> 02:30.567
Go brag about it
to the other grandmothers. Okay?

02:31.192 --> 02:32.610
Tell everybody, all right?

02:33.653 --> 02:34.487
All right.

02:36.239 --> 02:38.074
-[Heung-rye] Hawaii?
-Yeah.

02:38.658 --> 02:42.370
I told her it wasn't worth the bother,
but dear Ka-young insisted on a vacation

02:42.453 --> 02:44.998
and booked the flights just like that!
Non-refundable.

02:45.081 --> 02:48.209
-So, I have to go.
-How rich is she?

02:48.293 --> 02:50.211
Working like that on cars?

02:50.920 --> 02:54.132
-I guess she saved everything she could.
-[laughs]

02:54.215 --> 02:57.802
You must be getting your good karma
in one fell swoop. I'm so jealous.

02:58.428 --> 03:00.513
When do you leave?
Take some kimchi with you.

03:00.597 --> 03:02.557
-I've heard the food is heavy.
-On Monday.

03:02.640 --> 03:06.477
Oh, you know, I'm heading
to the market today to get what I need.

03:06.561 --> 03:08.396
Does anyone want me to pick up anything?

03:08.479 --> 03:12.650
She's heading to Seoul tonight. You didn't
forget we're seeing the doctor, did you?

03:12.734 --> 03:16.112
The only trips you book for me
are appointments with that damn doctor.

03:16.195 --> 03:18.740
Why don't you ever
book a flight to Hawaii?

03:18.823 --> 03:22.035
[Da-jin] My goodness. [claps]
All right, everyone, class has begun.

03:22.118 --> 03:24.746
Let's start with a nice, big stretch.

03:24.829 --> 03:25.830
Up!

03:25.914 --> 03:27.206
[Bok-ja groans]

03:27.290 --> 03:29.626
-And to your right.
-Oh, my right.

03:30.835 --> 03:32.170
Oh. Manager Kang.

03:32.253 --> 03:33.504
[line ringing]

03:33.588 --> 03:35.173
Manager Kang, hello.

03:35.256 --> 03:38.426
It appears Ka-young
is taking Pan-geum to Hawaii.

03:38.968 --> 03:41.888
She's had a hard time,
but I'm glad she gets a vacation.

03:42.472 --> 03:45.016
If you want a vacation,
you could see if your son will take you.

03:47.018 --> 03:48.978
[chuckles] Oh, no. I couldn't, no.

03:49.729 --> 03:52.482
-Can't have him splurge on little ol' me.
-[line rings]

03:52.565 --> 03:54.442
-[sighs]
-[line rings]

03:54.525 --> 03:58.488
I'll have your sister-in-law do
the ancestral rites, so don't you worry.

03:58.571 --> 04:00.823
-[line ringing]
-All right.

04:01.532 --> 04:05.745
I won't be able to attend anyway.
I'm supposed to go to Seoul for Jeong-hwa.

04:06.496 --> 04:07.330
What?

04:07.872 --> 04:09.457
Why, is everything all right?

04:09.540 --> 04:11.334
[line rings]

04:15.046 --> 04:16.506
[Im-seon] Where the hell are you?

04:16.589 --> 04:18.925
[Jeong-hwa] I'm at the prep academy.
Where else would I be?

04:19.008 --> 04:22.762
Well, I'm at your place right now.
You thought I'd never swing by here?

04:23.346 --> 04:25.139
-Ugh.
-I swear, I am ending your lease!

04:25.223 --> 04:27.433
Is this why you never wanted me here?

04:29.018 --> 04:31.771
[shouts] Do you know what the hell
I just found in your trash?

04:31.854 --> 04:34.816
You're pissing me off! Who gave you
permission to snoop through my stuff?

04:34.899 --> 04:36.442
[scoffs] Permission?

04:36.526 --> 04:38.278
Do you even go to class?

04:38.361 --> 04:40.863
Right. Well,
I was gonna tell you anyway.

04:40.947 --> 04:44.117
I want to stop prepping for the college
exam. I'm not gonna go to college.

04:44.200 --> 04:46.202
Oh, you're just not going?

04:46.995 --> 04:50.248
[scoffs] Tell me how you're gonna
make it in life without college?

04:50.915 --> 04:52.041
Tell me how.

04:52.125 --> 04:54.085
Tell me how you'll manage,
help me understand!

04:54.168 --> 04:56.087
I can still have a good life
without school!

04:56.671 --> 04:59.757
Do you even know the privileges you enjoy?

04:59.841 --> 05:01.259
-I'm hanging up!
-[line disconnects]

05:01.342 --> 05:02.343
Hello?

05:03.720 --> 05:05.013
Yoo Jeong-hwa!

05:05.972 --> 05:07.849
-God! How could she!
-[cell phone clatters]

05:07.932 --> 05:11.352
Seriously. [sobbing]

05:21.279 --> 05:23.656
God, back when I was just a cashier…

05:24.657 --> 05:27.869
[sniffles] we practically never fought.

05:30.288 --> 05:32.040
Oh, my little girl.

05:32.123 --> 05:34.000
[Iblis] You can always go back, you know?

05:34.083 --> 05:36.627
[Im-seon sobbing]

05:36.711 --> 05:38.421
You have one wish remaining.

05:39.630 --> 05:40.923
You could undo it all.

05:45.178 --> 05:46.179
[sniffles]

05:46.262 --> 05:48.514
[ominous music playing]

05:48.598 --> 05:49.599
[breath shudders]

05:51.100 --> 05:52.935
I can't just waste it on that.

05:54.771 --> 05:56.439
It's too valuable.

05:59.609 --> 06:00.485
It is.

06:02.028 --> 06:03.029
[chuckles quietly]

06:03.905 --> 06:07.992
-[watch ticking]
-1,044, 1,045,

06:08.076 --> 06:11.245
1,046, 1,047.

06:16.793 --> 06:18.294
What the… Where is he?

06:20.129 --> 06:21.130
Where is he?

06:21.714 --> 06:23.174
[whooshing]

06:24.926 --> 06:27.553
[groaning]

06:27.637 --> 06:30.014
Hey, where have you been?
Why weren't you on time?

06:30.098 --> 06:32.433
Deadline's in 15 seconds.
My wish fulfilled?

06:32.517 --> 06:33.434
[scoffs]

06:35.019 --> 06:35.853
Are you blind?

06:37.105 --> 06:39.065
We still have three seconds to go.

06:39.148 --> 06:42.235
[watch ticking thrice]

06:43.111 --> 06:44.445
[alarm chimes]

06:45.196 --> 06:46.280
[energy chimes]

06:48.366 --> 06:50.451
[suspenseful music playing]

06:50.535 --> 06:53.663
[Iblis] Your second wish
has now been fulfilled.

07:01.420 --> 07:03.673
-Grandma, you asleep?
-[cell phone clatters]

07:05.258 --> 07:09.095
Oh, dear. What time is it?
Is it already time to go to the airport?

07:09.679 --> 07:13.015
Oh, my goodness.
I haven't even finished packing yet.

07:14.350 --> 07:15.226
[groans]

07:15.768 --> 07:18.312
What in the world?
How did this come loose?

07:20.148 --> 07:21.149
[sighs]

07:22.442 --> 07:24.569
We should take kimchi
and gochujang, right?

07:24.652 --> 07:26.654
[music intensifies]

07:30.950 --> 07:31.868
Grandma.

07:33.244 --> 07:35.746
-You were pretty.
-What are you saying?

07:36.330 --> 07:38.833
I'm swollen,
I fell asleep right after dinner.

07:39.667 --> 07:41.085
[clears throat]

07:41.794 --> 07:42.920
Why is my voice…

07:43.004 --> 07:45.590
You are so much prettier
than I ever imagined.

07:45.673 --> 07:48.134
I just woke up. What is this?

07:48.217 --> 07:51.512
Where do you think your face came from?
It all started here. [chuckles]

07:52.472 --> 07:55.266
Ah, yeah, let's see, let's see.

07:55.850 --> 07:59.061
We should at least have a few boiled eggs
before we go, right?

08:00.146 --> 08:02.398
[yelps, gasps] Oh, she startled me.

08:03.191 --> 08:04.942
Who's this? This a friend of yours?

08:05.026 --> 08:07.445
No. You know I have
no other friends than Min-ji.

08:08.196 --> 08:09.155
Then who is that?

08:12.325 --> 08:14.577
I've seen that face before.

08:16.120 --> 08:17.705
She's so familiar.

08:17.788 --> 08:19.790
[suspenseful music plays]

08:21.626 --> 08:23.002
My God.

08:23.878 --> 08:25.755
[gasps] Am I…

08:26.881 --> 08:29.217
-Is this a dream or what?
-You could say that.

08:29.926 --> 08:31.135
Do you know who that is?

08:33.054 --> 08:34.972
[breath trembling]

08:36.557 --> 08:38.601
[gasping]

08:40.811 --> 08:42.230
I know this face.

08:43.731 --> 08:46.984
This… This beautiful young face
belongs to…

08:47.068 --> 08:49.445
[gasping]

08:49.529 --> 08:53.157
Uh, if you faint, do it to your left.

08:54.116 --> 08:54.951
[groans]

08:58.246 --> 08:59.163
[gasps]

09:00.206 --> 09:03.751
The young lady who had her pick
of every eligible boy.

09:03.834 --> 09:05.294
[gasps, groans]

09:07.171 --> 09:09.966
I can wear a fancy outfit
from my grandbaby's closet!

09:10.508 --> 09:13.219
Even squeeze into
a pair of pointy heels! [sighs]

09:14.262 --> 09:18.474
[gasping] Oh, goodness! Lord Buddha!

09:18.558 --> 09:23.271
Gods above and below!
Virgin Mary! Thank you!

09:23.354 --> 09:24.772
-[groans]
-[body thuds]

09:26.691 --> 09:28.568
It wasn't any of them.

09:29.360 --> 09:31.696
-It was someone from the Middle East.
-[scoffs smugly]

09:32.405 --> 09:33.823
[dramatic music plays]

09:33.906 --> 09:37.076
I know what this is. It's that notebook.
Your writing.

09:37.159 --> 09:38.869
-Wishes!
-Yeah.

09:38.953 --> 09:41.330
So, it's real? It won't undo overnight?

09:44.208 --> 09:45.167
[chuckles excitedly]

09:45.251 --> 09:47.169
Uh… [sighs]

09:48.671 --> 09:49.839
[gasps]

09:51.882 --> 09:53.593
Grandma? What are you doing?

09:54.343 --> 09:57.138
Which one's the Chanel? [gasping]

09:57.221 --> 09:59.432
[hangers clacking]

09:59.515 --> 10:01.434
[birds cawing]

10:07.440 --> 10:08.274
Really?

10:09.317 --> 10:12.028
I'm surprised so much occurred
in such a small town.

10:15.489 --> 10:16.407
[grunts]

10:18.951 --> 10:19.869
[Ejllael exhales]

10:19.952 --> 10:23.414
Am I mistaken or have you
been exercising more lately?

10:23.497 --> 10:26.208
I might be deploying my wings more
in the coming days. [pants]

10:28.044 --> 10:29.378
My clothes keep tearing.

10:29.462 --> 10:31.631
So, you're just not gonna wear anything?

10:31.714 --> 10:35.009
Manufacturing one piece of clothing
uses 7,000 liters of water.

10:35.092 --> 10:37.511
So you plan to just fly naked.

10:37.595 --> 10:40.222
[sighs] Focus. Anything to report?

10:41.307 --> 10:43.392
Ms. Ki Ka-young has made another wish.

10:43.476 --> 10:46.395
And it is indeed a noble one.
Congratulations.

10:47.021 --> 10:49.690
You know a noble wish
doesn't guarantee noble results.

10:50.441 --> 10:51.692
We need to stay vigilant.

10:53.527 --> 10:54.779
And Iblis, where is he?

10:55.863 --> 10:58.324
[Iblis] So what?
She made her grandma young.

10:58.407 --> 11:01.160
What about it?
That count as righteous? [scoffs]

11:01.827 --> 11:03.204
[sighs nervously]

11:04.288 --> 11:07.375
Whatever. Don't get obsessed
by such minor details.

11:07.458 --> 11:10.002
That market employee,
her first wish was wicked.

11:11.629 --> 11:13.714
Yeah. You're doing great.

11:15.675 --> 11:17.802
But why do you insist
on sitting like this?

11:17.885 --> 11:18.969
[groans] My back.

11:20.763 --> 11:23.516
[groaning]

11:29.021 --> 11:30.856
[tense music plays]

11:30.940 --> 11:33.859
When did I give you permission
to just waltz in here?

11:33.943 --> 11:36.529
Did I give you permission
to show up at my building?

11:38.656 --> 11:41.367
So Irem chirped away again. Hey.

11:41.951 --> 11:45.496
I imagine you're all excited about
Ki Ka-young making a righteous wish.

11:45.579 --> 11:48.290
But her first wish was still enough
for me to slit her throat.

11:48.374 --> 11:49.708
[scoffs] Blah, blah, blah.

11:49.792 --> 11:52.294
So, being that was born on Wednesday,
would you kindly let me

11:52.378 --> 11:54.713
continue my internal contemplations
and get the hell out?

11:54.797 --> 11:57.049
[laughs] Contemplations?

11:57.133 --> 12:00.302
Looked like panic to me, wouldn't you say,
Satan, born on Thursday?

12:00.386 --> 12:03.848
Huh? You think I… [laughing]

12:03.931 --> 12:07.226
Oh, if you were to analyze the faces
of the other two wishers,

12:07.309 --> 12:10.646
oh, it's so amazing.
They're all but guaranteed to be damned.

12:10.729 --> 12:14.817
Oh, and the dog?
Ooh, yeah, it's in the bag. Sorry, bro.

12:14.900 --> 12:17.111
Didn't I warn you
to stop disrupting the human world?

12:17.194 --> 12:19.155
A dog turns into a man
and you think that's that?

12:19.238 --> 12:21.449
-Meh, meh, meh, meh…
-An old lady becomes young again.

12:21.532 --> 12:24.577
What about everyone's memories, huh?
Giving them gold? How's that gonna work?

12:24.660 --> 12:28.122
You can't walk into a bank with massive
bags of gold without getting flagged!

12:28.205 --> 12:29.874
Your methods? They're really outdated.

12:30.458 --> 12:33.002
Face it.
You no longer have a purpose here.

12:33.085 --> 12:35.921
Well, even so, that's mean.

12:37.715 --> 12:38.841
You're just gassing.

12:39.341 --> 12:40.509
"Gaslighting."

12:40.593 --> 12:41.427
Oh.

12:42.636 --> 12:43.679
Sade, you idiot!

12:45.473 --> 12:48.267
And what if I can prove to you
I've got value?

12:48.851 --> 12:51.187
-[sighs]
-[man] Genie! Genie!

12:52.188 --> 12:54.607
Where are you? Mr. Genie, sir?

12:54.690 --> 12:56.066
Do your best to prove it, then.

12:57.151 --> 12:58.903
Everyone's gonna want you now.

12:59.778 --> 13:01.697
You better not disturb me
in my lamp again.

13:02.990 --> 13:04.783
Okay, I'm coming, dog!

13:04.867 --> 13:06.035
Where are you?

13:06.118 --> 13:07.578
[whooshing]

13:10.664 --> 13:14.084
Can you help me? I only know dog things.
[breathing shakily]

13:14.835 --> 13:18.631
I look like a human, you know?
But what can I do?

13:19.840 --> 13:22.009
Nothing. I'm hopeless.

13:22.593 --> 13:23.511
Help me.

13:23.594 --> 13:27.056
So, your second wish
is the same as your first wish?

13:27.640 --> 13:29.391
What's with the speech? [laughs]

13:29.475 --> 13:30.351
Is it a shtick?

13:30.434 --> 13:32.061
No, no. No, no, no, no, no.

13:32.144 --> 13:34.939
No, no, my father was
a show dog. High class.

13:35.648 --> 13:39.193
But I can't do anything
without, uh, money, uh, picture ID.

13:39.902 --> 13:42.738
-Money. A picture ID. I need them.
-[sighs]

13:44.907 --> 13:47.535
-[sniffing]
-I know how hard it is, buddy.

13:48.744 --> 13:50.871
Try being a genie to five wishers.

13:51.830 --> 13:52.748
[sniffing]

13:54.166 --> 13:56.126
-[sniffing]
-I also find it bewildering.

13:57.336 --> 13:59.171
Okay. Better idea.

14:00.172 --> 14:02.216
You'll be so powerful,
you don't even need an ID.

14:02.925 --> 14:05.886
Huh? What… What kind of person is that?

14:05.970 --> 14:07.596
A person who simply…

14:08.931 --> 14:11.225
hires others to carry ID for him.

14:11.308 --> 14:12.142
[snaps fingers]

14:12.226 --> 14:14.061
[upbeat music playing]

14:14.144 --> 14:16.063
GOBLIN STATIONERY

14:16.814 --> 14:19.567
[Iblis] The key is to have a tall man
with his hair slicked back,

14:19.650 --> 14:21.527
wearing a suit no matter the weather,

14:21.610 --> 14:23.737
come out of the driver's side of your car.

14:24.989 --> 14:28.826
And you?
Ha. You sit in the back seat.

14:32.413 --> 14:34.248
-Hey. Over there.
-[boy 1] Huh?

14:34.832 --> 14:37.626
-Wow.
-[boy 1] Wow, that's fucking cool.

14:37.710 --> 14:40.838
How'd that bastard end up
being driven around in a car like that?

14:40.921 --> 14:43.549
-That guy looks top dog.
-He must have worked like a dog.

14:44.133 --> 14:46.844
Maybe he'll throw us
a bone or something if we're lucky.

14:48.596 --> 14:50.514
[snarls]

14:56.395 --> 14:57.730
[boy 2] He's coming over here.

14:57.813 --> 14:59.940
[clicking tongue] Hey, assholes.

15:02.151 --> 15:06.071
You hit a dog. You beat one up
in this alley. Do you deny it? Huh?

15:06.780 --> 15:09.199
It was a cocker spaniel, right?

15:09.283 --> 15:10.951
Isn't that one of those crazy dogs?

15:11.994 --> 15:13.954
So what? [scoffs] Was that you?

15:14.038 --> 15:15.247
[laughs]

15:16.665 --> 15:20.169
Well, I guess.
You know who else is crazy? Hmm?

15:21.462 --> 15:23.297
-[growling]
-[boy 1] What the hell?

15:23.380 --> 15:25.215
-[yelping]
-Yo, hey! Leave him alone! Hey!

15:25.299 --> 15:27.760
-[boy 2] Fucking asshole!
-[boy 1] Get off, you crazy ass!

15:28.510 --> 15:29.845
Hey, you son of a bitch!

15:29.929 --> 15:33.140
-[growling]
-[yelping]

15:34.767 --> 15:35.893
[wincing]

15:37.937 --> 15:38.854
[boy 1 groans]

15:41.982 --> 15:45.569
Here, for your medical costs.
Don't ever mess with dogs.

15:46.779 --> 15:49.573
I'll keep an eye on you. [growls]

15:49.657 --> 15:52.034
-[boy 2] Hey. The cash. Grab it.
-[growls]

15:52.117 --> 15:53.619
Pick up the money, damn it!

15:56.038 --> 15:58.207
[sighs, gasps]

16:03.671 --> 16:05.214
-Oh, come on.
-[keypad beeping]

16:06.799 --> 16:08.384
[gasping]

16:08.926 --> 16:11.595
-[chiming and whooshing]
-[gasps]

16:12.721 --> 16:17.059
[Iblis] Four means death, so of course
the Angel of Death's passcode is 1004.

16:17.142 --> 16:19.478
So predictable. [cackles]

16:19.561 --> 16:22.106
-[tense comical music plays]
-[Ejllael gasping]

16:24.274 --> 16:25.192
[Ejllael] Ah, damn it.

16:26.652 --> 16:27.569
[sighs]

16:28.445 --> 16:31.949
Iblis, you satanic asshole!

16:33.283 --> 16:35.577
-[door slams]
-[running footsteps]

16:36.912 --> 16:37.871
Grandma?

16:41.125 --> 16:41.959
Grandma?

16:50.426 --> 16:51.260
[sighs]

16:54.888 --> 16:56.598
[muttering]

16:56.682 --> 16:57.516
[sighs]

16:58.183 --> 17:00.144
A leather jacket in summer?

17:00.227 --> 17:02.229
[peppy music plays]

17:03.147 --> 17:04.523
[humming]

17:09.278 --> 17:10.112
[gasps]

17:11.071 --> 17:12.114
[pants]

17:17.453 --> 17:18.537
Chanel.

17:20.539 --> 17:21.373
[grunts]

17:22.791 --> 17:25.002
[snaps fingers, chuckles]

17:35.095 --> 17:35.929
[giggles]

17:37.139 --> 17:38.265
Grandm--

17:40.476 --> 17:42.019
[giggles, gasps]

17:45.272 --> 17:46.607
[grunts softly]

17:47.941 --> 17:48.817
[scoffs]

17:51.236 --> 17:52.696
[panting]

17:54.073 --> 17:54.907
[Pan-geum gasps]

18:02.748 --> 18:05.209
I can breathe now. I'm not winded at all!

18:06.043 --> 18:08.170
And my back is fine too. [gasps]

18:09.213 --> 18:12.091
[giggles, squeals]

18:12.174 --> 18:13.175
[scoffs]

18:14.426 --> 18:15.344
[laughs]

18:17.596 --> 18:18.931
[engine revving]

18:19.640 --> 18:20.682
Grandma, watch out!

18:22.559 --> 18:23.727
[gasps]

18:24.603 --> 18:25.646
[exhales]

18:32.069 --> 18:32.903
You okay there, son?

18:34.863 --> 18:36.740
Young lady, watch where you're going.

18:37.616 --> 18:39.618
"Young lady"? [laughs heartily]

18:40.327 --> 18:42.663
"Young lady"? Whoo!

18:43.288 --> 18:45.582
I'm a young lady!

18:45.666 --> 18:46.792
-Whoo!
-[scoffs]

18:47.668 --> 18:49.419
-[comical music playing]
-[footsteps]

18:49.503 --> 18:51.338
[Pan-geum humming heartily]

18:52.089 --> 18:53.090
[gasping]

18:54.675 --> 18:56.468
Uh…

18:56.552 --> 18:59.138
[gasps, giggles]

18:59.221 --> 19:00.055
[gasps]

19:01.348 --> 19:02.683
Aw. [grunts]

19:04.810 --> 19:06.603
[Ka-young] Grandma needs some rules too.

19:07.437 --> 19:08.272
Mm.

19:08.856 --> 19:11.525
[Pan-geum humming]

19:12.442 --> 19:13.986
[gasps] Ooh.

19:14.611 --> 19:16.363
-You're not hot?
-[Pan-geum clears throat]

19:17.114 --> 19:20.075
No way. It's totally perfect. Why?

19:20.159 --> 19:21.285
Listen to me now.

19:21.910 --> 19:25.205
I'm going to relay some rules
that you must follow no matter what.

19:25.289 --> 19:27.124
First, do not answer this phone ever.

19:27.207 --> 19:30.752
Come on! I'm not an idiot.
My voice is as light as a bird.

19:30.836 --> 19:33.380
Of course I won't.
I'll use this new phone. What else?

19:33.463 --> 19:35.257
-Uh, hey, guys--
-Second.

19:35.340 --> 19:38.427
-If someone asks why you've come here?
-I'm just here to try out country life.

19:38.510 --> 19:39.720
Third rule. Origin?

19:41.555 --> 19:42.598
Hadong?

19:42.681 --> 19:45.976
-Hey, so, Ka-young?
-Hadong is also a country province, so no.

19:46.059 --> 19:47.811
You're from Cheongdam-dong, Seoul.

19:47.895 --> 19:51.565
-Your name is--
-Ooh, I already know. Lee Mi-ju. Nice, no?

19:51.648 --> 19:54.484
Great. And then, from now on,
you talk modern.

19:55.068 --> 19:57.446
This stays between him, you and me.

19:58.363 --> 20:01.158
So stick to the rules
and don't get caught. Can you do that?

20:01.241 --> 20:03.744
Really. I'm not a moron.

20:03.827 --> 20:04.912
When I was young…

20:05.704 --> 20:07.664
Actually, I'm young now.

20:08.248 --> 20:12.044
Hey, so, uh, just wondering
what we're having for dinner tonight.

20:12.127 --> 20:14.254
Stop thinking about food.
You don't even need to eat!

20:15.047 --> 20:17.341
-Grandma, can you speak young?
-Pshh.

20:19.593 --> 20:22.930
[gasps] Oh, my goodness!
I get so startled every time he does that.

20:25.724 --> 20:29.019
I mean, I am for real bugging at that guy.

20:29.102 --> 20:32.731
Anyway, when I was young,
I was cool and ambitious.

20:34.608 --> 20:36.777
Is a salon mandatory
when applying for the Miss Korea?

20:36.860 --> 20:39.446
You'd be cut because you don't have
the right eyelids.

20:39.529 --> 20:42.366
Look, just go to the salon,
try something new.

20:43.075 --> 20:45.202
What if I got
some plastic surgery? [gasps]

20:45.827 --> 20:47.579
Why is she so stingy?

20:48.330 --> 20:49.873
I don't even eat that much. Pshh.

20:50.499 --> 20:51.333
[scoffs]

20:52.668 --> 20:54.670
Wow, this young man sure is early.

20:54.753 --> 20:57.464
Seems like a strong one too.
He'll for sure get picked.

20:57.547 --> 20:58.757
-Yeah, move over.
-Scooch.

20:59.383 --> 21:00.842
-Great. Thank you.
-Oh, hey.

21:00.926 --> 21:02.010
-Oh, hey.
-Shove down.

21:02.094 --> 21:04.054
[man] Here, here. Yeah, that's it.

21:04.137 --> 21:06.515
-Uh, wait--
-Scooch down, a little more.

21:06.598 --> 21:07.599
Don't fall off the edge.

21:08.308 --> 21:11.853
All right, everyone. I need 15 people
to work the cabbage patch today.

21:11.937 --> 21:14.022
[men] Me! Me! Me!

21:14.106 --> 21:16.525
What the…
You don't like this bench either?

21:16.608 --> 21:18.860
-[man] Me! Me! Me!
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

21:18.944 --> 21:21.571
I don't like this bench either. Hey!

21:22.364 --> 21:23.949
I agree, this bench isn't big enough.

21:26.493 --> 21:27.828
[workers grunting]

21:40.340 --> 21:42.301
[energetic music playing]

21:42.384 --> 21:44.553
[Iblis grunting]

21:47.347 --> 21:48.390
[man] Come on, lunch time!

21:49.057 --> 21:51.059
[indistinct chatter]

21:55.772 --> 21:57.566
Mm. Scrumptious.

22:04.156 --> 22:05.782
You dined and dashed? Huh?

22:06.491 --> 22:09.578
Huh, my goodness.
Thanks to you, we're almost done.

22:10.329 --> 22:11.496
[chuckles] Here.

22:13.123 --> 22:15.042
-Oh, what's…
-It's your pay for today.

22:16.376 --> 22:18.503
-I get money?
-Huh. [chuckles]

22:19.212 --> 22:20.839
-Oh, my.
-Wow.

22:22.674 --> 22:25.093
[comical music plays]

22:25.177 --> 22:26.470
Oh, you're here too?

22:26.553 --> 22:27.387
Sit, sit.

22:27.471 --> 22:30.474
-Yeah, scoot over. Yeah.
-Oh.

22:32.267 --> 22:33.852
-Hi.
-[man] You're back again?

22:33.935 --> 22:35.145
Hi, Mr. Kim. [chuckles]

22:39.691 --> 22:41.568
-[tires screech]
-[crashing]

22:41.651 --> 22:42.694
[thudding]

22:48.909 --> 22:51.078
[breathing laboriously]

23:03.340 --> 23:04.341
[Sang-tae] What is this?

23:05.884 --> 23:07.094
[lamp thuds]

23:08.678 --> 23:10.472
[deer breathing laboriously]

23:13.183 --> 23:15.519
How fucking annoying. Ugh.

23:17.354 --> 23:19.106
You should have just died.

23:21.566 --> 23:22.818
-[wind gusting]
-[groans]

23:28.240 --> 23:31.034
What-- Who are you? Where did you--

23:35.997 --> 23:38.458
-You saw me?
-Yes, I saw everything.

23:38.542 --> 23:39.960
And it's totally irrelevant.

23:40.544 --> 23:42.921
I'm a genie of the lamp.
I shall grant you three wishes.

23:43.004 --> 23:45.257
No bringing back the dead.
No traveling to the future.

23:45.340 --> 23:48.051
Anything other than that,
your wish is my command.

23:49.052 --> 23:51.054
Um, sir, are you drunk?

23:51.638 --> 23:53.265
Just continue on your merry way.

23:53.348 --> 23:55.976
I'm only letting you live
because you're a guy.

23:57.310 --> 24:00.397
You can see my form? Damn!
I came as myself, I was distracted.

24:00.480 --> 24:03.817
I would've been picked first for the
cabbage patch, so hurry and make a wish.

24:04.317 --> 24:05.610
What the fuck? [chuckles]

24:06.153 --> 24:08.488
This imbecile out at the crack
of dawn, what gives?

24:09.114 --> 24:10.240
So you're a genie?

24:11.491 --> 24:13.326
Then bring this thing back to life.

24:14.244 --> 24:16.830
I'm pleased with your efficiency.

24:16.913 --> 24:19.457
I can heal it because it's still alive.
[grunts softly]

24:20.333 --> 24:21.543
[energy humming]

24:27.257 --> 24:28.842
[deer grunts]

24:30.051 --> 24:31.761
-[gasps]
-There it goes.

24:31.845 --> 24:33.805
Do you need to think
about your second wish

24:33.889 --> 24:35.599
or shall we push ahead?

24:35.682 --> 24:38.476
Ah, shit! Fuck!

24:40.061 --> 24:43.440
This is real? That's seriously twisted!

24:43.523 --> 24:46.776
[panting] Why didn't you tell me
it was real, you bastard?

24:47.360 --> 24:50.614
I just used a wish on nothing,
motherfucker!

24:50.697 --> 24:52.407
[grunts, pants]

24:53.533 --> 24:55.952
-[engine revs]
-[tires screech]

24:56.036 --> 24:58.038
[yelps, gasping]

25:05.378 --> 25:06.546
Why, you little!

25:08.131 --> 25:12.052
I'm your master, right? I control you!
You can't do this shit!

25:12.135 --> 25:14.471
Oh, yeah? Says who? That's just a myth.

25:14.971 --> 25:17.641
I grant your wishes,
but I can also be quite awful.

25:21.269 --> 25:22.437
Like this.

25:23.104 --> 25:25.023
[groaning]

25:28.360 --> 25:31.279
Wait. Wait, wait, wait. Wait a second.
Let's just hold on here.

25:32.530 --> 25:34.324
That means I got two wishes remaining.

25:42.415 --> 25:43.250
Huh?

25:45.418 --> 25:47.921
Why is the lamp not there? Where is it?

25:48.004 --> 25:51.424
Only when you know your greatest desire
will the lamp appear.

25:52.342 --> 25:54.678
Give it careful consideration
before next time.

25:54.761 --> 25:57.264
You're just a lump of clay,
so you'll never control me.

25:58.306 --> 26:01.977
Oh, this? Next time,
my face will be different.

26:03.228 --> 26:05.063
So don't waste energy memorizing it.

26:06.064 --> 26:07.148
[laughs]

26:09.109 --> 26:10.485
[panting]

26:13.488 --> 26:17.909
Son of a bitch! [panting]

26:18.868 --> 26:20.120
[Da-jin] Good morning,
everyone.

26:20.203 --> 26:23.206
It's a gorgeous day,
so we're going to plant lettuce heads.

26:23.290 --> 26:26.876
I'm sure there are a lot of you
that have insomnia, huh? I do too.

26:26.960 --> 26:29.504
So I decided to wake up
and plant these to… [snarls playfully]

26:29.587 --> 26:31.589
eat 'em up so I can sleep better.

26:31.673 --> 26:36.594
All right. So, baby lettuce needs
to be planted 20 centimeters apart.

26:36.678 --> 26:38.430
We'll plant one right here…

26:39.472 --> 26:41.766
and another one over here. Like that.

26:42.475 --> 26:43.393
And here.

26:45.645 --> 26:46.479
Uh…

26:46.563 --> 26:48.481
YOU'RE GOING TO KEEP ME UP AT NIGHT!

26:48.565 --> 26:50.191
I think I'm going to sign off now.

26:50.775 --> 26:53.403
-I'll do another live when the crops grow.
-Huh? Hey.

26:53.486 --> 26:54.321
Hey, hold on.

26:55.071 --> 26:55.905
[sighs]

26:56.781 --> 26:58.908
What happened?
We were getting so much traffic.

26:59.409 --> 27:01.202
-You zoomed in again.
-Huh?

27:02.495 --> 27:05.457
Oh, um, well, you leaned over,
so… [chuckles]

27:06.041 --> 27:08.543
-What? You bastard!
-[grunts, groans]

27:10.253 --> 27:11.546
Here's my left cheek.

27:13.006 --> 27:16.801
Ugh, they say sex sells! Mm.

27:18.553 --> 27:19.929
Ugh, you son of a bitch!

27:20.013 --> 27:21.973
-I'm gonna kill you for that!
-Ow! Wait! No! Stop!

27:22.057 --> 27:23.016
[upbeat music playing]

27:23.099 --> 27:26.186
[Sade] So, I looked into it.
You know the sleazy guy?

27:26.269 --> 27:31.441
Turns out, she and him met at this
top university, the famous science one.

27:31.524 --> 27:33.276
Really? They met how?

27:34.569 --> 27:35.862
[sighs, pants]

27:36.488 --> 27:37.989
A club for waltzing.

27:38.948 --> 27:39.824
What?

27:41.576 --> 27:42.452
Waltzing?

27:43.453 --> 27:45.663
[classical waltz music playing]

27:54.464 --> 27:57.926
I will say, I never thought of you
as someone who waltzed.

27:58.009 --> 27:59.302
I didn't before.

27:59.969 --> 28:02.514
I was told my a friend
to try breaking down dance moves

28:02.597 --> 28:04.057
instead of breaking down skulls.

28:05.100 --> 28:07.185
[laughs]

28:07.268 --> 28:09.187
Wow, you really are bizarre.

28:09.771 --> 28:12.732
By the way, I saw you turned down
that scholarship.

28:12.816 --> 28:15.360
And because of you,
I get to study overseas.

28:15.443 --> 28:18.196
The Arab League, doing research.
I'm grateful.

28:18.279 --> 28:22.242
Don't mention it. I've got money,
so I can always pay my own way if I do go.

28:22.826 --> 28:26.162
Didn't you say you're from a village
in Chungcheong-do?

28:26.246 --> 28:27.956
Our chilies are growing well lately.

28:31.376 --> 28:34.003
Gosh, you're so… [laughing]

28:38.508 --> 28:40.427
[music continues]

28:41.678 --> 28:44.055
[slows to a stop]

28:44.639 --> 28:45.765
-Whatever.
-I know, right?

28:45.849 --> 28:47.100
-[man] Buddy!
-Jun-u!

28:47.183 --> 28:48.435
-Whoa!
-Oh, man.

28:49.394 --> 28:51.187
-[groaning in pain]
-You okay?

28:51.271 --> 28:53.106
-What'd you trip on? You okay?
-What is it?

28:53.606 --> 28:54.983
-What's wrong?
-It's true.

28:55.567 --> 28:58.445
-You did fall in a very strange way.
-What's gotten into you?

29:00.280 --> 29:01.197
[gasps]

29:01.281 --> 29:03.992
Is your face okay? Or was it
already like that before you fell?

29:04.075 --> 29:05.118
What's up with this bast--

29:05.201 --> 29:08.121
Oh, you're hurt. Don't bother trying
to answer your buddies.

29:08.204 --> 29:11.416
Man, is that painful?
Do you think it's broken?

29:12.125 --> 29:13.835
-[bones crackle, snap]
-[Jun-u groaning]

29:13.918 --> 29:16.921
[classical waltz music playing]

29:31.227 --> 29:32.061
[knock on door]

29:34.773 --> 29:35.648
Guests outside.

29:40.945 --> 29:42.781
[Chang-sik] Mm. Mm.

29:46.284 --> 29:48.411
[Jong-heon] What is up
with this creepy house?

29:49.996 --> 29:51.289
You gonna talk to all of them?

29:52.040 --> 29:55.210
You know, it doesn't really seem like
a typical household.

29:55.293 --> 29:57.003
-Mm?
-Mm. Don't be cowards.

29:57.587 --> 29:59.130
-It's fine.
-[gasps]

29:59.214 --> 30:00.381
-You chicken?
-Mm.

30:01.299 --> 30:04.427
Well, what a ludicrously large family.
Are you all brothers?

30:05.512 --> 30:06.679
Dad was very busy, eh?

30:06.763 --> 30:09.349
-Anyway, can I speak to him?
-What can I do for you?

30:10.475 --> 30:13.311
Ah. Sorry we didn't say hello sooner.

30:13.394 --> 30:15.814
In any case, uh,
I'm the village chief of Cheongpung--

30:15.897 --> 30:17.524
I said, what can I do for you?

30:18.149 --> 30:19.150
[unsettling music plays]

30:19.234 --> 30:23.488
Oh. Well, we heard you moved in,
but we hadn't heard from you yet.

30:24.155 --> 30:25.865
You've to complete
the new resident intake,

30:25.949 --> 30:27.700
but we didn't know
your family was so large.

30:27.784 --> 30:29.327
I don't think we have enough forms.

30:29.410 --> 30:31.621
Local news is broadcast
on the Band channel,

30:31.704 --> 30:33.623
so make sure to subscribe to it, yeah?

30:35.375 --> 30:36.626
Put your info in.

30:38.837 --> 30:41.923
Goodness, I forgot.
I'd lose my head if it wasn't attached.

30:42.006 --> 30:44.342
-Your name is?
-It's Jung Jun-u. Hey.

30:45.260 --> 30:46.594
Put your contact info in here.

30:46.678 --> 30:49.806
[unsettling music continues]

30:54.394 --> 30:56.521
Oh, we still have other things to go over.

31:02.485 --> 31:03.319
[gasps]

31:05.989 --> 31:06.990
Damn, what the hell?

31:15.832 --> 31:18.543
-What's up?
-I'm protecting Grandma.

31:19.544 --> 31:23.172
Everything rides on this staying secret.
Check if the signal is coming through.

31:23.673 --> 31:24.591
That your final wish?

31:24.674 --> 31:27.010
If you're not going to help me, screw off.

31:27.093 --> 31:28.303
Oh!

31:29.095 --> 31:30.179
That your final wish?

31:32.473 --> 31:34.058
Why're you going on about wishes again?

31:35.268 --> 31:38.229
I grew up beautiful. Without scars either.

31:41.816 --> 31:43.902
Isn't that what you said to me
when I was eight?

31:45.528 --> 31:47.071
Ever heard of white lies?

31:47.697 --> 31:50.366
All lies are bad.
They rob you of an opportunity to grow.

31:50.450 --> 31:54.704
Oh! Is that why you're installing
spy cameras in the middle of the night?

31:54.787 --> 31:56.623
Because you're so honest? Ha!

32:07.842 --> 32:09.427
[both panting]

32:17.060 --> 32:19.812
Hey. You stopped barking, huh?

32:24.108 --> 32:27.362
[Mi-ju grunts] I know I buried it here.
Where is it?

32:27.445 --> 32:29.614
[pants, grunts]

32:29.697 --> 32:31.032
Come on, darn it!

32:32.617 --> 32:33.576
[Ka-young] Hmm.

32:33.660 --> 32:35.620
-There's no money there.
-[gasping]

32:35.703 --> 32:37.205
Hasn't been for a decade.

32:37.288 --> 32:39.332
Don't sneak around like that.

32:39.415 --> 32:40.917
I nearly had a heart attack.

32:41.000 --> 32:43.711
Your heart's too young now
to have a heart attack.

32:43.795 --> 32:46.339
I dug up all the cash you buried,
gave it away.

32:47.298 --> 32:51.052
But you… you… How did you know about it?

32:51.135 --> 32:53.262
Wait, wait. It's all gone?

32:54.347 --> 32:56.683
-Just the principal.
-Just the principal?

32:59.769 --> 33:00.937
[gasping]

33:02.105 --> 33:06.150
So, you're saying there's more.
Hand it over. We'll share the profit.

33:06.859 --> 33:09.487
Grandparents are usually paid
for childcare these days, hmm?

33:09.570 --> 33:12.407
I've made… too much to share.

33:13.157 --> 33:16.494
-I've earned a fortune in stocks.
-Stocks?

33:18.788 --> 33:20.540
That document you had me sign?

33:21.124 --> 33:24.460
[Min-ji] I mean, what high schooler
thinks to do such aggressive investing?

33:26.754 --> 33:30.174
[sighs] I saw all those stocks
you bought skyrocketing

33:30.258 --> 33:32.301
and thought you were possessed
or whatever.

33:32.385 --> 33:34.595
But, hey, then you paid
for my college tuition.

33:34.679 --> 33:36.889
My mom thought you were amazing.

33:37.473 --> 33:40.935
You made her wishes comes true.
You were like a god to her.

33:41.019 --> 33:44.856
So incredible. I'm finally getting out
of this town! I can't wait!

33:44.939 --> 33:45.940
You still eating?

33:46.858 --> 33:49.485
Well, yeah. The food just came out,
so I'm still eating.

33:51.029 --> 33:52.989
Uh, what are you looking at?

33:53.072 --> 33:54.907
-Something going on?
-I need to get home now.

33:54.991 --> 33:58.119
Why? Is it because of that jerk?

33:58.202 --> 34:01.372
I told you not to get too serious
with some asshole you don't even know.

34:02.665 --> 34:04.876
Hey. You still here?

34:04.959 --> 34:08.296
Weren't you going to Hawaii
with your grandma? Are you still going?

34:09.630 --> 34:13.509
Uh, I decided I was too busy to go,
but Grandma still went.

34:13.593 --> 34:17.847
Uh, she wanted to try out her new
swimsuit, so we decided she'd go alone.

34:17.930 --> 34:20.600
Alone? Oh. Hmm.

34:20.683 --> 34:23.061
Why is it so hard then
to get her on the phone?

34:23.561 --> 34:25.104
The flight is really long,

34:25.188 --> 34:28.149
and she didn't wanna set up
international calling on her phone.

34:28.232 --> 34:30.860
Your grandma is on her way
to Hawaii? Alone?

34:31.694 --> 34:34.155
My goodness! You are always so selfish!

34:34.238 --> 34:36.407
Why not give your spot to someone, huh?

34:36.491 --> 34:40.703
You could have given your ticket to me.
Did it just go to waste? [tutting]

34:40.787 --> 34:43.081
Hey, have my order boxed up to go.

34:43.164 --> 34:45.917
This one is incapable
of ever thinking of others.

34:46.000 --> 34:47.877
You need to watch your reputation.

34:47.960 --> 34:51.380
Oh, a box to go.
I'll get the rest of this to go too.

34:52.131 --> 34:54.675
-I'm gonna eat my meal at home.
-You're going?

34:54.759 --> 34:56.761
But I'm still eating!

34:56.844 --> 34:59.222
SOYEON SALON

34:59.806 --> 35:00.640
[sighs]

35:02.767 --> 35:03.935
[scooter approaching]

35:04.560 --> 35:06.521
-Move, move, move, move!
-[Min-ji] Watch out!

35:07.563 --> 35:09.774
[Mi-ju gasping]

35:09.857 --> 35:12.151
[intriguing music playing]

35:15.530 --> 35:18.491
Hey, you brat!
You almost ran over this woman!

35:18.574 --> 35:19.867
I saw your face!

35:19.951 --> 35:21.202
[chuckles]

35:22.745 --> 35:25.331
-You all right?
-Oh, thank you!

35:25.414 --> 35:28.000
My darling Min-ji saved me!

35:28.084 --> 35:29.585
[gasps, sighs]

35:31.129 --> 35:32.713
Just wow.

35:33.464 --> 35:35.299
-We know each other?
-Uh…

35:36.759 --> 35:41.180
You own the dental clinic over there!
Of course I've heard of you!

35:41.764 --> 35:44.016
Oh. Uh, Lee Mi-ju.

35:44.767 --> 35:46.602
I've come to live in the country
for a spell.

35:46.686 --> 35:50.064
Everyone said to visit Smile Dental Clinic
if I ended up in Cheongpung village.

35:50.148 --> 35:52.024
I was wondering when to visit. [chuckles]

35:52.108 --> 35:53.818
Is that so? [chuckles]

35:53.901 --> 35:55.653
Well, please do come, whenever.

35:56.362 --> 35:59.448
But I gotta say, there's not a lot
to fix. Your smile's great.

35:59.532 --> 36:03.494
[gasps] Oh, my goodness,
my teeth got younger too!

36:03.578 --> 36:06.164
Oh, you're from Gyeongsang-do, aren't you?

36:06.247 --> 36:08.166
When did you move? Where are you staying?

36:09.167 --> 36:10.585
Oh, well, I…

36:12.378 --> 36:16.340
[chuckles] Well, we're bound
to cross paths like this again.

36:16.424 --> 36:17.842
If fate allows it.

36:18.426 --> 36:19.927
[laughs] Yeah, okay.

36:20.928 --> 36:23.472
Oh, if you're thinking
of getting a new hairdo,

36:23.556 --> 36:26.058
you have a great jaw,
keep the volume.

36:26.142 --> 36:29.103
Don't cut it. Just get a blowout
if you want more character.

36:33.566 --> 36:34.442
Oh. Oh.

36:37.486 --> 36:38.613
[sighs in relief]

36:40.323 --> 36:43.492
A hairdo?
In what world could I pay for that?

36:43.576 --> 36:46.621
I can just straighten
my hair myself at home. [scoffs]

36:48.289 --> 36:49.999
But you only live once.

36:51.626 --> 36:52.752
[bell jingles]

36:59.508 --> 37:01.135
I heard you have something to share.

37:01.677 --> 37:02.720
Oh, nothing major.

37:03.888 --> 37:05.514
You went to school
with that Ki Ka-young?

37:07.516 --> 37:08.726
We weren't really close.

37:09.810 --> 37:12.480
-[girl] What's for lunch today?
-[indistinct chatter]

37:13.606 --> 37:15.107
[manager] You may
not have been close,

37:15.191 --> 37:17.193
but you weren't strangers, right?

37:18.611 --> 37:20.571
Do I have to spell it out for you?

37:20.655 --> 37:22.865
Can't I just trust you
to take charge of anything?

37:22.949 --> 37:26.202
All right, look. You know how we launched
a new pension product?

37:26.911 --> 37:30.414
The only VIP we have who has the means
to quality for that pension product

37:30.498 --> 37:31.499
is Miss Ki Ka-young.

37:32.500 --> 37:35.503
You could go and see her
and do some, you know… Hmm?

37:36.170 --> 37:38.089
Come on, be proactive, spearhead this!

37:38.756 --> 37:40.091
I'll need time to think about it.

37:40.174 --> 37:42.677
[slaps table] Jeez,
why waste time thinking about it?

37:42.760 --> 37:45.638
I've already done all the thinking,
you just need to do it.

37:47.098 --> 37:50.476
Figure out your strategy
over the weekend, all right? Hmm?

37:51.936 --> 37:52.770
[clears throat]

37:54.480 --> 37:55.481
[door opens]

37:57.733 --> 38:00.069
-[door closes]
-[breath shuddering]

38:00.152 --> 38:02.738
[somber music playing]

38:11.372 --> 38:12.206
[soap squirts]

38:13.874 --> 38:16.210
-[scrubbing vigorously]
-[grunts]

38:19.505 --> 38:20.339
[gasps]

38:20.881 --> 38:23.175
[huffs] What's this?

38:27.138 --> 38:29.515
Who the hell makes tea
and doesn't even clean the kettle?

38:30.683 --> 38:33.019
[chiming]

38:33.102 --> 38:35.479
[yelping]

38:36.981 --> 38:40.151
What the… [coughing] Is this asbestos?

38:40.860 --> 38:42.486
[coughing]

38:43.404 --> 38:45.406
[magical music playing]

38:51.620 --> 38:54.332
[echoing] I am a genie of the lamp.

38:55.166 --> 38:57.668
I shall grant you three wishes. Make them.

38:58.711 --> 39:02.006
No reanimating the dead.
And no going to the future.

39:03.049 --> 39:04.342
-Otherwise--
-A genie?

39:05.051 --> 39:05.968
Mm?

39:07.887 --> 39:10.348
-Um, I'm not quite done explaining.
-[chuckles]

39:11.098 --> 39:13.059
-[laughing]
-Mm?

39:13.142 --> 39:16.187
[Bo-gyeong laughing excitedly]

39:19.065 --> 39:21.025
I am special! I knew it!

39:21.108 --> 39:24.028
I knew a day like this would come
if I just held on!

39:24.612 --> 39:28.199
-It normally takes a lot longer than this.
-I know my first wish!

39:28.282 --> 39:29.283
Uh, my first wish…

39:30.451 --> 39:32.745
There's a girl called Ki Ka-young.
She runs a garage.

39:32.828 --> 39:34.955
[tense music builds]

39:36.791 --> 39:37.958
Go on.

39:38.042 --> 39:41.045
GU BO-GYEONG
JUNE 20, 2024

39:41.128 --> 39:43.464
MADE HER FIRST WISH

39:44.465 --> 39:46.592
Okay. Tell me what her first wish was.

39:48.302 --> 39:50.179
Hurry up. I need to go demand a refund.

39:50.971 --> 39:53.599
-Can't you see I'm in my refund outfit?
-"Refund outfit"?

39:53.682 --> 39:56.685
I bought an eight-piece tool set,
and the fourth tool isn't there.

39:56.769 --> 39:58.104
The fourth is my favorite.

39:59.105 --> 40:00.022
Unacceptable.

40:02.441 --> 40:04.985
Wouldn't blood red be nice
on a white outfit?

40:05.069 --> 40:06.487
So hurry up already.

40:07.071 --> 40:08.906
Tell me what Gu Bo-gyeong's wish was.

40:10.783 --> 40:15.413
I want you to transfer every cent
Ki Ka-young has in her account over to me.

40:17.164 --> 40:19.041
So you want lots of money
like Ki Ka-young has.

40:19.125 --> 40:20.376
No, no.

40:21.001 --> 40:24.255
I want her wealth, all of it.
Her money. Now!

40:26.090 --> 40:27.258
I want what she has.

40:28.259 --> 40:29.093
Huh.

40:30.219 --> 40:31.053
Ah.

40:32.847 --> 40:34.682
You want to bring her misfortune.

40:36.725 --> 40:37.560
Hmm.

40:38.227 --> 40:39.186
[inhales sharply]

40:40.062 --> 40:41.897
What to do?

40:43.399 --> 40:45.276
[energy hums]

40:51.699 --> 40:52.867
It is done.

40:53.742 --> 40:54.660
It-- It is?

40:55.828 --> 40:56.829
[cell phone chimes]

40:58.789 --> 41:00.541
DEPOSIT, KI KA-YOUNG
10,000,000 WON

41:00.624 --> 41:02.835
[gasps, sobs in delight]

41:04.503 --> 41:06.505
[squeals]

41:06.589 --> 41:08.257
What would you like for your next wish?

41:08.340 --> 41:10.217
Oh, oh, just a minute, just a minute.

41:10.885 --> 41:13.387
I don't need to make
my next wish right away, do I?

41:14.221 --> 41:16.307
[chuckles] Right now…

41:19.101 --> 41:21.395
I would just like to indulge
in my new wealth.

41:28.736 --> 41:30.821
[Iblis] Ki Ka-young,
who said all humans are kind,

41:30.905 --> 41:32.448
has appeared in someone else's wish.

41:32.531 --> 41:33.949
You sure about humans?

41:34.033 --> 41:36.827
It is quite infuriating
that she went in that direction.

41:38.204 --> 41:39.663
Still, you did win that one.

41:42.374 --> 41:44.835
Kang Im-seon, Eom Sang-tae, Gu Bo-gyeong.

41:45.961 --> 41:49.048
I will say, it's looking quite likely
that I'll be winning this bet.

41:49.131 --> 41:51.759
WANTED EVERYTHING
IN KI KA-YOUNG'S ACCOUNT, EVERY LAST CENT

41:53.093 --> 41:53.969
All right.

41:57.848 --> 41:59.433
It does indeed look that way.

42:02.811 --> 42:03.646
So don't move.

42:08.275 --> 42:10.528
[gentle music plays]

42:10.611 --> 42:11.445
Uh…

42:12.780 --> 42:13.948
What are you doing?

42:15.908 --> 42:18.619
You asked to be treated with care.
This is showing you care.

42:18.702 --> 42:20.037
I can't do this if I lose.

42:24.583 --> 42:27.127
Oh, my dear spirit of the lamp is warm.

42:28.254 --> 42:30.422
Sweet little Satan is so brave.

42:32.883 --> 42:34.718
My dear Iblis is so warm.

42:41.016 --> 42:42.518
[energy chiming]

42:48.440 --> 42:50.442
[gentle music continues]

43:01.120 --> 43:02.371
Say, I've been wondering.

43:03.872 --> 43:06.959
How come the hourglass doesn't flow?
How can you even tell time?

43:07.626 --> 43:09.336
Because it's an urn, not a clock.

43:10.754 --> 43:11.839
That's you in there.

43:13.048 --> 43:14.717
I took a handful of you.

43:15.634 --> 43:16.468
An urn?

43:17.553 --> 43:18.387
[Iblis grunts]

43:25.394 --> 43:26.312
[Ka-young sighs]

43:27.521 --> 43:29.356
Never knew an urn
could be this scaled down.

43:29.440 --> 43:30.274
[stomps]

43:30.357 --> 43:33.027
I can't even get my coffin
any smaller than a mailbox.

43:33.902 --> 43:35.696
Hey, we were so cozy just now.

43:36.739 --> 43:38.449
Why you freezing me out like that?

43:43.746 --> 43:46.248
[Ka-young] Did you hold
ancestral rites for me?

43:46.332 --> 43:49.335
-[energy humming]
-[suspenseful music plays]

43:54.840 --> 43:55.924
-[rapid ticking]
-Huh?

43:56.008 --> 43:57.635
[music intensifies]

44:00.387 --> 44:01.305
[gasps]

44:03.974 --> 44:06.977
[indistinct shouting]

44:07.061 --> 44:09.938
-Cast the Goryeo bitch aside too!
-Please.

44:13.025 --> 44:14.568
[laughing]

44:17.363 --> 44:18.906
[gasps]

44:22.618 --> 44:23.452
What's wong?

44:24.495 --> 44:27.456
I've dreamt of that girl.
She is me after all.

44:29.833 --> 44:31.752
I've seen this place in my dreams too.

44:33.128 --> 44:34.672
It's a bit different.

44:36.006 --> 44:38.467
Yes, but still. [gasps]

44:39.885 --> 44:41.011
I was laughing here.

44:41.512 --> 44:42.805
Uh, what?

44:43.681 --> 44:46.350
I've never had you here,
not once in any of your past lives.

44:47.768 --> 44:49.186
It could be the future.

44:49.853 --> 44:50.813
But I'm sure of it.

44:51.730 --> 44:53.524
I was laughing, like…

44:57.444 --> 44:58.362
In that creepy way?

45:03.659 --> 45:05.411
Hey, where did you hide my toolbox?

45:13.919 --> 45:15.337
Should've gone to a service center.

45:15.421 --> 45:18.590
If I notice any issues,
I'm going to have to order the parts in,

45:18.674 --> 45:19.925
so it'll be a while.

45:20.008 --> 45:22.261
That's okay. Just do a standard once-over.

45:23.095 --> 45:25.264
Wait here a sec,
I'm gonna dash to the bank real quick.

45:35.983 --> 45:39.278
Stop watching me.
I don't like people staring.

45:40.612 --> 45:41.697
[spray hisses]

45:46.785 --> 45:49.705
Is it okay for an adult
to be so blunt to a child?

45:49.788 --> 45:51.498
Think you're special 'cause you're young?

45:53.000 --> 45:56.253
-Go sit over there and read.
-I've already finished my book.

45:56.336 --> 45:57.212
HISTORY OF GORYEO

45:57.296 --> 45:59.715
During the Goryeo dynasty,
they referred to Arabia as Saracen

45:59.798 --> 46:01.258
and had prominent trade routes.

46:01.341 --> 46:03.510
But the trade stopped after the year 1040.

46:04.094 --> 46:06.472
They didn't say why.
I guess the path was blocked?

46:06.555 --> 46:07.973
Well, I didn't do it.

46:08.056 --> 46:10.184
You know "Double Flower Shop"?
That old song?

46:10.767 --> 46:14.313
I heard some say that the "father" they
sing about is really an Arabian merchant,

46:14.396 --> 46:16.356
who went all the way
to Goryeo from Arabia.

46:16.440 --> 46:19.860
Surely there are merchants who went
to Arabia from Goryeo, don't you think?

46:19.943 --> 46:22.029
Go ask the Internet about this,
not a repair shop.

46:22.112 --> 46:23.113
[footsteps]

46:23.697 --> 46:24.823
Oh, what now?

46:25.908 --> 46:28.911
-Hey, apprentice!
-[panting]

46:28.994 --> 46:31.955
-You rang, Ms. Ki?
-Watch the shop, okay?

46:32.039 --> 46:34.082
Did she have to steal my favorite heels?

46:38.295 --> 46:40.297
[suspenseful music plays]

46:48.180 --> 46:49.723
[grunts] Wait.

46:51.058 --> 46:52.226
[pants]

46:58.065 --> 47:01.151
[pop music playing over speakers]

47:03.153 --> 47:04.196
[exhales]

47:04.780 --> 47:06.198
[Mi-ju] Mm, let's see.

47:09.576 --> 47:11.411
Goodness, how does this work?

47:13.247 --> 47:15.832
-Oh.
-You definitely should try this one.

47:16.458 --> 47:19.127
So we meet again. Like fate.

47:19.211 --> 47:21.755
[chuckles] This town is so small.

47:22.631 --> 47:23.715
Please, you first.

47:24.466 --> 47:26.385
Oh, so you're not getting coffee?

47:26.468 --> 47:27.761
You never used a kiosk before?

47:27.844 --> 47:29.346
Ah, well, uh…

47:29.429 --> 47:31.682
Ah, someone always took care
of that for you.

47:32.432 --> 47:33.850
What kind of guys did that?

47:35.185 --> 47:37.479
-[giggles]
-This coffee is better with an extra shot.

47:38.897 --> 47:39.731
[giggles]

47:40.732 --> 47:41.775
You laugh a lot.

47:43.694 --> 47:46.071
I'm grateful. And you're so sweet.

47:46.154 --> 47:48.156
That's a pretty bold thing to throw out.

47:48.865 --> 47:50.867
Did you get a blowout? Pretty.

47:51.785 --> 47:53.787
Oh, this blowout isn't pretty.

47:54.663 --> 47:55.872
It's-- Ah!

47:55.956 --> 47:59.042
Ooh, I know. It's 'cause my clothes
are doing all the work. [chuckles]

47:59.126 --> 48:00.127
Your clothes?

48:01.128 --> 48:01.962
No.

48:03.130 --> 48:06.133
Huh? [laughing]

48:09.678 --> 48:11.179
-[chuckles]
-Oh, goodness.

48:12.180 --> 48:13.348
[Iblis] Whatcha doing?

48:14.933 --> 48:16.810
[Ka-young] Monitoring Grandma.

48:16.893 --> 48:18.437
I see her smiling.

48:18.520 --> 48:19.563
Look.

48:20.147 --> 48:21.398
Real happiness.

48:22.649 --> 48:23.483
Why?

48:24.401 --> 48:26.445
She was her own person in her youth.

48:26.528 --> 48:28.113
[laughing]

48:28.864 --> 48:29.823
Shit.

48:30.741 --> 48:33.160
Why doesn't she live with her, then? Huh?

48:34.161 --> 48:35.120
[Ka-young scoffs]

48:35.912 --> 48:37.080
[Iblis] Uh, by the way…

48:38.915 --> 48:40.792
When you showed me care the other day…

48:41.877 --> 48:43.420
so what are the rules with that?

48:44.171 --> 48:48.884
Is it the time, or the location,
or the day, or the outfit?

48:49.426 --> 48:52.012
[sighs] Is that really
what you're thinking about?

48:52.888 --> 48:54.598
I feel like trash, so stop talking to me.

49:00.270 --> 49:01.438
[scoffs]

49:10.030 --> 49:12.741
[groans] I can't do it right! Ahh!

49:16.745 --> 49:17.996
This isn't cool!

49:18.789 --> 49:21.833
[whines] Iblis!

49:22.918 --> 49:24.086
[groans]

49:27.297 --> 49:28.131
[Iblis groans]

49:29.049 --> 49:31.551
-[Iblis] Why is nothing coming out?
-[whooshing]

49:35.472 --> 49:37.808
[sighs] Come with me.

49:38.809 --> 49:40.310
[Iblis] Whoa!

49:40.394 --> 49:41.228
[grunts]

49:42.354 --> 49:44.981
[rousing music playing]

49:54.408 --> 49:57.619
You, you emptied out everything
in my safe,

49:57.703 --> 50:01.248
and gave all that money
to that dirty mutt.

50:01.873 --> 50:03.709
Just being practical.

50:05.460 --> 50:07.796
It was the only money
that wouldn't get him flagged.

50:08.964 --> 50:10.298
Oh, and he's not a mutt.

50:11.258 --> 50:15.387
His father was a show dog
with a British pedigree. [laughs]

50:16.680 --> 50:17.514
[sighs]

50:28.734 --> 50:30.902
[sighs] Why did you carve out the eyes?

50:30.986 --> 50:34.406
Oh… Well, that was
the original painting, right?

50:35.198 --> 50:36.783
The original? [yells] The original?

50:37.659 --> 50:39.119
You damn well know it wasn't!

50:41.455 --> 50:43.874
[sighs] I'm at my wit's end.

50:46.084 --> 50:49.171
[uptempo rock music plays]

50:49.254 --> 50:50.547
[yells]

50:51.923 --> 50:53.884
[yelping]

50:57.763 --> 50:58.722
Oh, dear.

50:59.639 --> 51:01.266
[laughing]

51:02.684 --> 51:03.602
[mockingly] Oh.

51:10.150 --> 51:12.903
-[Iblis grunts]
-[yelling]

51:16.281 --> 51:17.741
[Ejllael groans]

51:27.834 --> 51:29.461
[both panting]

51:37.385 --> 51:39.179
-[strains]
-[Iblis] Game over.

51:39.721 --> 51:43.517
Ten, nine… [laughs]

51:45.227 --> 51:47.896
Iblis! [grunts]

52:00.075 --> 52:02.494
[laughing]

52:24.766 --> 52:26.059
Please.

52:26.643 --> 52:28.728
[Ka-young] Please, what? A sword?

52:28.812 --> 52:30.522
-Please.
-A sickle?

52:30.605 --> 52:32.315
-Please.
-An ax?

52:32.399 --> 52:33.358
Please.

52:36.903 --> 52:40.824
[Ka-young] I was probably asking for
a sword to cut someone's head off. Yeah.

52:40.907 --> 52:43.910
[birds cawing]

52:46.288 --> 52:47.122
[sighs]

52:50.417 --> 52:53.628
-[loud, clamored cawing]
-[ominous music plays]

53:08.602 --> 53:10.645
What are you doing at my house at night?

53:11.897 --> 53:13.690
You better not be here for my grandma.

53:14.900 --> 53:16.234
If you are, I'll kill you.

53:16.318 --> 53:18.737
You may be Iblis' master,
but you cannot kill me.

53:19.529 --> 53:21.448
And I'm here to see you, Ms. Ki Ka-young.

53:21.531 --> 53:22.532
Me?

53:24.326 --> 53:26.661
-Am I to die?
-[chuckles] No. Mm-mm.

53:27.954 --> 53:29.331
That won't be happening just yet.

53:31.333 --> 53:33.543
I know you've already made
your second wish.

53:35.545 --> 53:38.173
[sighs] What exactly makes that
any of your concern?

53:41.343 --> 53:45.347
I thought I could provide some assistance
on deciding your final wish.

53:45.430 --> 53:46.973
[suspenseful music playing]

53:49.893 --> 53:54.189
Do you know the exact reason
Iblis wants to kill you?

53:54.272 --> 53:58.276
I trapped him for a thousand years.
I'm pretty sure that's why.

53:58.860 --> 54:02.072
Precisely. And what was the reason
for your first death?

54:06.076 --> 54:07.243
Don't you want to know?

54:11.164 --> 54:12.874
Would you like to learn the truth?

54:14.292 --> 54:15.669
To come with me…

54:18.463 --> 54:19.965
to the moment of your death?

54:21.424 --> 54:23.718
[dramatic music plays]

54:24.719 --> 54:27.138
[birds cawing]

54:33.395 --> 54:35.772
[dramatic rock fusion music plays]
